WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501
-I'm so happy
we're finally meeting in person.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been a fan of yours
for a long time.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:07.173
The piece that I think first
put you on my radar is in 2014.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:10.010
You were covering a Donald Trump
speech in New Hampshire.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.480
This is when he was sort
of pretending to be a politician

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
or somebody
who might run for office.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.784 line:92%
-You then, because of a storm,

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.754 size:88% position:44%
you ended up flying back
with him to Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you wrote an article
about those 36 hours.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.826
-I spent 36 hours marooned
at Mar-a-Lago with Donald Trump.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yes, I wrote a profile
[chuckles]

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
a 6,000-word story
about that time with him that,

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
suffice it to say,
he didn't not like.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.637
But the piece --
kind of the gist of the piece --

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
because my whole takeaway
from him at that time

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.777
was that he was almost like
a tragic figure, you know?

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:44.444 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He wanted so desperately

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
for me to take him seriously
as a political figure,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I didn't.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. You --
-You know?

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.553
I know you can't relate to that.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah, exactly.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I want to get to
our similarities.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:58.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you forward the article,
which was for BuzzFeed --

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.893 line:92%
you mocked up like a joke...

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was the joke picture...
-This -- Yeah.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.430 line:92%
...of him in the Oval Office,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:07.734
and that's like
what it [bleep] looks like now.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.802 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:12.472
So I do want to get back
to the parallels we have,

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.141
which is that was sort of
a piece like you are --

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.309 line:92%
you did not take him seriously.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
In 2011,
at the Correspondents' Dinner,

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:21.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "You know, your --
it's a joke.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:21.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your running is a joke."
-Yeah.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How motivated as he is --
is he by dopes like us?

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well --
Well, this is the thing.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.487 line:92%
I've -- We never met before,

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.989 size:81% position:41%
but I've always felt
this kinship with you,

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we're like
part of this fraternity

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
of haters and losers...
-Yeah.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...who questioned
Donald Trump's seriousness

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as a candidate.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:42.001
The thing that I've learned
about Donald Trump is that,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:42.936 line:92%
even though he was born with

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.538
all the wealth and privilege
he possibly could have had,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.307 line:92%
even though he's now president,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.007 size:78% position:39% line:92%
he's always felt like

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
he kind of has his face
pressed up against the glass.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he feels like
he's an outsider

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that nobody
takes him seriously enough,

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.882 size:75% position:38% line:92%
no one respects him.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
The insiders
are all sneering at him.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.320 size:88% position:44%
I was actually told once
during the election --

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was after --
or right around the time

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.525
he was winning the primaries --
that I --

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.893 line:92%
that article that I wrote

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:10.463 size:84% position:42%
was one of the reasons
that he decided to run.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:13.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
But -- But
that adviser told me that --

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is
a former Trump adviser --

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
told me that
you were higher on the list...

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, well that --
-...on that list of reasons.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
So...
-That...

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.710 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.211 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So...

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause
continue ]

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:32.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he -- never let it be said
he is not a vengeful man --

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that -- right? --

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.921
is it the night of
the convention he e-mailed you?

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just -- Just a couple days
before the convention,

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.826
before he formally accepted
the Republican nomination,

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.862
I got an e-mail from him saying,
you know,

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.797 line:92%
"McKay, you got it all wrong.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:48.201
And just watch what's gonna
happen in the general election."

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "You got this all wrong.
I can't believe it."

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:53.106
That was what was going through
his mind,

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.542
you know, as he's winning
the Republican primary.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:59.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's -- I think that people
don't understand

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
just how much
this matters to him,

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.283 line:92%
just how much it matters to him

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:06.286
to prove the haters wrong,
to prove everyone wrong.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:09.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even now, when he's in the --
in the Oval Office,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.525
one of the things
that reporters are dealing with

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.726 line:92%
when they cover this White House

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.061 line:92%
is that you'll write a story

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's well sourced,
that's accurate

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
about some staffer
who's gonna be fired.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:23.036
And because Trump will see it
reported, he'll change his mind,

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to be able to say,
"Look, that was fake news.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got them wrong."
-Right.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.976
-He's really motivated
by trying to disprove the press,

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.580
to disprove anybody who he
thinks is unfairly treating him.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.382
-I want to talk about sourcing
real quick because, you know,

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.485
it seems like we hear so much
coming out of this White House,

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than, maybe,
we've ever had --

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:42.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
we've ever heard.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is because,
from the very top,

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
he is a source that he is
talking to the press so often

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.630
that the people underneath him
feel the freedom to do the same?

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, absolutely.
You know, it's funny.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
Trump does this thing where,

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.536 line:92%
after his day's work is done,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:59.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
he'll retire to the Residence
of the White House

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just kind of make
freewheeling phone calls

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
to, like, random people.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, sometimes, they're,
like, fellow billionaire pals,

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:07.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, sometimes,
they're media people,

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, sometimes,
they're reporters.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And it's funny --
I've had experiences with this

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.354
even when I was interviewing him
at Mar-a-Lago

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he'll be talking,
and he'll tell you a story,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.725
and he'll be like, "Okay,
this part's off the record.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, now this part, just
attribute it to someone else,"

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.028 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or whatever.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'll just --
he'll -- he'll be --

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:26.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
he'll just put random stuff
out there.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.066 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And that --

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:30.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of the stories you see
in -- in the press are --

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
it'll say like "somebody
familiar with the situation,"

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.041
or like
"a senior White House official,"

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.810
and it'll be the
President of the United States.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:41.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lurking, slow-moving
mass of a man.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.684
[ Laughter ]
Did -- And do you think, like --

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that actually seems like
he's thinking about it

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:47.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
more than
we maybe give him credit for.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.189
So, while he's telling a story,
he is at least aware enough

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.426
to know which parts to pull off
the record and on the record.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, in my experience,
at least,

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:58.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was the parts
that he wanted me to write

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.132 line:92%
that were flattering about him,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he didn't want
to have it attributed to him.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:02.568 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Got it.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:05.004
-So, it'll be
like some heroic story about him

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.005 line:92%
or a story about some celebrity

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:09.309
who said he was the greatest
ever of something, you know.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
"But -- But
put that off the record.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.779 line:92%
Just don't use my name on that."

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.681
-So he wants it out there,
but he wants it to seem like

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:17.850
it came from another source.
-He wants -- Exactly. Right.

